12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the closed-loop voltage gain expressions for Inverting and Non-Inverting operational amplifier configurations using the Virtual Ground concept.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Derivation of Inverting and Non-Inverting Closed-Loop Gain:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operational Amplifier Ideal Assumptions:) Tj
T*
(   - Infinite input impedance \(Rin -> infinity => zero input bias current: I+ = I- = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Infinite open-loop voltage gain \(Aol -> infinity\).) Tj
T*
(   - Finite output voltage requires: Vout = Aol * \(V+ - V-\) => \(V+ - V-\) = Vout / Aol = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Virtual Short / Summing Point Constraint: V- = V+.) Tj
T*
(   2. Inverting Amplifier Configuration:) Tj
T*
(   - Non-inverting terminal grounded: V+ = 0 V => V- = 0 V \(Virtual Ground\).) Tj
T*
(   - Input signal Vin connected through series resistor R1 to inverting terminal.) Tj
T*
(   - Feedback resistor Rf connected between output Vout and inverting terminal.) Tj
T*
(   - Applying KCL at inverting node:) Tj
T*
(   I1 = \(Vin - V-\) / R1 = \(Vin - 0\) / R1 = Vin / R1.) Tj
T*
(   If = \(V- - Vout\) / Rf = \(0 - Vout\) / Rf = - Vout / Rf.) Tj
T*
(   - Since op-amp draws zero current \(I- = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   I1 + If = 0 => Vin / R1 + \(- Vout / Rf\) = 0 => Vin / R1 = Vout / Rf.) Tj
T*
(   - Closed-Loop Gain:) Tj
T*
(   Av = Vout / Vin = - \(Rf / R1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Negative sign indicates an exact 180-degree phase inversion. Input impedance is Rin = R1.) Tj
T*
(   3. Non-Inverting Amplifier Configuration:) Tj
T*
(   - Input signal Vin applied directly to non-inverting terminal: V+ = Vin.) Tj
T*
(   - By virtual short: V- = V+ = Vin.) Tj
T*
(   - Resistor R1 connected from inverting node to ground; feedback Rf from output to inverting) Tj
T*
(   node.) Tj
T*
(   - Applying KCL at inverting node:) Tj
T*
(   \(0 - V-\) / R1 + \(Vout - V-\) / Rf = 0 => - Vin / R1 + \(Vout - Vin\) / Rf = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Vout / Rf = Vin / R1 + Vin / Rf = Vin * [ \(R1 + Rf\) / \(R1 * Rf\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Closed-Loop Gain:) Tj
T*
(   Av = Vout / Vin = \(R1 + Rf\) / R1 = 1 + \(Rf / R1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Strictly positive \(zero phase shift\) with minimum gain of 1.0 \(when Rf = 0\). Input impedance) Tj
T*
(   is exceptionally high \(~infinity\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the 3-Op-Amp Instrumentation Amplifier: Derive the closed-loop differential gain and explain its superior Common Mode Rejection Ratio.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   3-Op-Amp Instrumentation Amplifier:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architectural Topology:) Tj
T*
(   - Input Stage: Two non-inverting buffer amplifiers \(A1 and A2\) cross-coupled by a single) Tj
T*
(   gain-setting resistor Rg, with feedback resistors R.) Tj
T*
(   - Output Stage: A high-precision balanced difference amplifier \(A3\) with four matched resistors) Tj
T*
(   \(R2, R3\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Differential Gain:) Tj
T*
(   - Let inputs be V1 \(at A1\) and V2 \(at A2\).) Tj
T*
(   - By virtual short concept: potential at inverting node of A1 is V1, and at inverting node of) Tj
T*
(   A2 is V2.) Tj
T*
(   - Current through gain resistor Rg:) Tj
T*
(   I_g = \(V1 - V2\) / Rg.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
