(Lovely Professional University | Biotechnology Question Bank & Solutions) Tj
340 0 Td
(Page 13 of 27) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   - Because no current enters op-amp inputs, current I_g flows through both feedback resistors R) Tj
T*
(   in series:) Tj
T*
(   Output of A1: Vo1 = V1 + I_g * R = V1 + R * \(V1 - V2\) / Rg.) Tj
T*
(   Output of A2: Vo2 = V2 - I_g * R = V2 - R * \(V1 - V2\) / Rg.) Tj
T*
(   - Differential output of input buffer stage:) Tj
T*
(   Vo1 - Vo2 = \(V1 - V2\) + 2 * R * \(V1 - V2\) / Rg = \(V1 - V2\) * [ 1 + \(2 * R / Rg\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - The buffer stage amplifies differential signal \(V1 - V2\) by factor [ 1 + 2*R/Rg ].) Tj
T*
(   - For common-mode signals \(V1 = V2 = Vcm\): I_g = 0; hence Vo1 = Vo2 = Vcm. Common-mode gain of) Tj
T*
(   input stage is strictly 1.0!) Tj
T*
(   - Output Difference Stage \(A3\):) Tj
T*
(   Vout = \(R3 / R2\) * \(Vo2 - Vo1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total Overall Closed-Loop Gain:) Tj
T*
(   Vout = \(R3 / R2\) * [ 1 + \(2 * R / Rg\) ] * \(V2 - V1\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Why Instrumentation Amplifiers Have Superior CMRR:) Tj
T*
(   - The first stage amplifies differential signals with high gain while passing common-mode noise) Tj
T*
(   with unity gain \(gain = 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Thus, the ratio of differential signal to common-mode signal is multiplied by [1 + 2*R/Rg]) Tj
T*
(   BEFORE reaching the difference stage.) Tj
T*
(   - Provides CMRR exceeding 100-120 dB even with minor resistor tolerances; extremely high input) Tj
T*
(   impedance prevents sensor loading.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
