T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the basic Op-Amp Integrator and Differentiator, explain their frequency-domain limitations, and design practical compensated versions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Op-Amp Integrators and Differentiators:) Tj
T*
(   1. Basic Inverting Integrator:) Tj
T*
(   - Input branch: Resistor R. Feedback branch: Capacitor C.) Tj
T*
(   - Time domain: i\(t\) = Vin\(t\) / R = - C * dVout/dt => Vout\(t\) = - \(1 / RC\) * Integral Vin\(t\) dt.) Tj
T*
(   - Transfer Function: H\(s\) = - 1 / \(s * R * C\) = - 1 / \(j * omega * R * C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Frequency Limitation: At DC \(omega -> 0\), |H\(0\)| -> infinity! The circuit acts as an) Tj
T*
(   open-loop amplifier for DC offsets; input offset voltage Vio charges capacitor C continuously,) Tj
T*
(   driving output into hard positive or negative saturation.) Tj
T*
(   - Practical Compensated Integrator: Place a large shunt resistor Rf in parallel with C. Rf) Tj
T*
(   clamps the DC closed-loop gain to -Rf/R, stabilizing the circuit. Integration is performed) Tj
T*
(   accurately for frequencies f >> 1 / \(2*pi*Rf*C\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Basic Inverting Differentiator:) Tj
T*
(   - Input branch: Capacitor C. Feedback branch: Resistor R.) Tj
T*
(   - Time domain: i\(t\) = C * dVin/dt = - Vout\(t\) / R => Vout\(t\) = - R * C * \(dVin / dt\).) Tj
T*
(   - Transfer Function: H\(s\) = - s * R * C = - j * omega * R * C.) Tj
T*
(   - Frequency Limitation: Gain |H\(j*omega\)| = omega * R * C increases linearly with frequency) Tj
T*
(   without bound \(+20 dB/decade\). High-frequency noise is amplified massively, completely) Tj
T*
(   obscuring the desired signal. Furthermore, internal op-amp poles add phase lag, producing 180 +) Tj
T*
(   90 = 270 deg phase shift, inducing severe instability and oscillation.) Tj
T*
(   - Practical Compensated Differentiator: Insert a small series resistor R1 in series with input) Tj
T*
(   capacitor C, and a small feedback capacitor Cf in parallel with Rf. The circuit behaves as a) Tj
T*
(   differentiator at low frequencies and rolls off as a low-pass filter at high frequencies,) Tj
T*
(   ensuring complete noise immunity and stability.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
