(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Op-Amp Schmitt Trigger and Hysteresis Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Inverting Schmitt Trigger:) Tj
T*
(   - Input voltage Vin is applied to the INVERTING terminal.) Tj
T*
(   - Positive feedback voltage divider \(R1 from non-inverting terminal to ground, R2 from) Tj
T*
(   non-inverting terminal to output Vout\).) Tj
T*
(   - Output saturates at either +Vsat or -Vsat.) Tj
T*
(   - Threshold Voltages at Non-Inverting Terminal \(V+\):) Tj
T*
(   By voltage divider: V+ = Vout * [ R1 / \(R1 + R2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - When Vout = +Vsat:) Tj
T*
(   Upper Threshold Voltage: V_UT = + Vsat * [ R1 / \(R1 + R2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - When Vout = -Vsat:) Tj
T*
(   Lower Threshold Voltage: V_LT = - Vsat * [ R1 / \(R1 + R2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Switching Dynamics:) Tj
T*
(   * Starting with Vin < V_LT: Vout = +Vsat.) Tj
T*
(   * As Vin increases, Vout remains +Vsat until Vin crosses V_UT. Once Vin > V_UT, output snaps) Tj
T*
(   instantaneously to -Vsat.) Tj
T*
(   * To switch back, Vin must decrease all the way below V_LT.) Tj
T*
(   - Hysteresis Width:) Tj
T*
(   V_H = V_UT - V_LT = 2 * Vsat * [ R1 / \(R1 + R2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   2. Non-Inverting Schmitt Trigger:) Tj
T*
(   - Inverting terminal grounded \(0 V\).) Tj
T*
(   - Input Vin connected via R1 to non-inverting terminal; positive feedback R2 from Vout to) Tj
T*
(   non-inverting terminal.) Tj
T*
(   - Switching occurs when V+ crosses 0 V:) Tj
T*
(   V+ = \(Vin * R2 + Vout * R1\) / \(R1 + R2\) = 0 => Vin * R2 = - Vout * R1.) Tj
T*
(   Vin = - Vout * \(R1 / R2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Upper Threshold \(switching from -Vsat to +Vsat\): V_UT = + Vsat * \(R1 / R2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Lower Threshold \(switching from +Vsat to -Vsat\): V_LT = - Vsat * \(R1 / R2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Hysteresis: V_H = 2 * Vsat * \(R1 / R2\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Purpose of Hysteresis:) Tj
T*
(   - Creates a deadband of width V_H. Any noise spikes smaller than V_H superimposed on slow or) Tj
T*
(   noisy analog waveforms cannot trigger false output transitions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
