(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the transfer function and design equations of a Second-Order Low-Pass Sallen-Key Active Butterworth Filter.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Second-Order Sallen-Key Low-Pass Active Filter:) Tj
T*
(   1. Circuit Topology:) Tj
T*
(   - Input Vin connected to resistor R1, followed by series resistor R2 connected to non-inverting) Tj
T*
(   op-amp terminal.) Tj
T*
(   - Capacitor C1 connected from junction of R1-R2 to op-amp output \(bootstrap positive feedback\).) Tj
T*
(   - Capacitor C2 connected from non-inverting terminal to ground.) Tj
T*
(   - Op-amp configured as non-inverting amplifier with gain K = 1 + \(Rb / Ra\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Nodal Derivation of Transfer Function:) Tj
T*
(   - Let internal node between R1 and R2 be Vx. Potential at non-inverting pin is V+ = Vout / K.) Tj
T*
(   - Applying KCL at node Vx:) Tj
T*
(   \(Vin - Vx\) / R1 + \(Vout - Vx\) * s*C1 + \(V+ - Vx\) / R2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Applying KCL at non-inverting node V+:) Tj
T*
(   \(Vx - V+\) / R2 = V+ * s*C2 => Vx = V+ * \(1 + s*R2*C2\) = \(Vout / K\) * \(1 + s*R2*C2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting Vx into node Vx equation and simplifying:) Tj
T*
(   H\(s\) = Vout\(s\) / Vin\(s\) = K / [ s^2 * R1*R2*C1*C2 + s * [ C2*\(R1 + R2\) + R1*C1*\(1 - K\) ] + 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Canonical Second-Order Form:) Tj
T*
(   - H\(s\) = K * omega_0^2 / [ s^2 + \(omega_0 / Q\) * s + omega_0^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Natural frequency: omega_0 = 1 / sqrt\(R1 * R2 * C1 * C2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Quality factor Q: 1 / Q = sqrt\(R2*C2 / R1*C1\) + sqrt\(R1*C2 / R2*C1\) + \(1 - K\) * sqrt\(R1*C1 /) Tj
T*
(   R2*C2\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Butterworth Filter Design \(Equal Component Strategy R1=R2=R, C1=C2=C\):) Tj
T*
(   - omega_0 = 1 / \(R * C\) => fc = 1 / \(2 * pi * R * C\).) Tj
T*
(   - 1 / Q = 1 + 1 + \(1 - K\) = 3 - K => Q = 1 / \(3 - K\).) Tj
T*
(   - For maximally flat Butterworth response, Q must equal 1 / sqrt\(2\) = 0.7071:) Tj
T*
(   3 - K = sqrt\(2\) => K = 3 - sqrt\(2\) approx 1.5858.) Tj
T*
(   - Setting feedback resistors: Rb / Ra = K - 1 = 0.5858.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
