/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the KHN \(Kerwin-Huelsman-Newcomb\) State-Variable Active Filter and its biquadratic tuning properties.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   KHN State-Variable \(Biquad\) Active Filter:) Tj
T*
(   1. System Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Composed of two op-amp inverting integrators and one summing/difference amplifier connected) Tj
T*
(   in a multi-loop feedback topology.) Tj
T*
(   - Directly models an analog computer solving a second-order differential equation:) Tj
T*
(   d^2 y/dt^2 + \(omega_0 / Q\) * dy/dt + omega_0^2 * y = f\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Universal Simultaneous Outputs:) Tj
T*
(   - Output 1 \(Summing amplifier output\): High-Pass Filter \(HPF\) response:) Tj
T*
(   H_HP\(s\) = s^2 / [ s^2 + \(omega_0 / Q\)*s + omega_0^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Output 2 \(First integrator output\): Band-Pass Filter \(BPF\) response:) Tj
T*
(   H_BP\(s\) = - \(omega_0 * s\) / [ s^2 + \(omega_0 / Q\)*s + omega_0^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Output 3 \(Second integrator output\): Low-Pass Filter \(LPF\) response:) Tj
T*
(   H_LP\(s\) = omega_0^2 / [ s^2 + \(omega_0 / Q\)*s + omega_0^2 ].) Tj
T*
