BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the Wein-Bridge Oscillator: Derive the condition for oscillation and frequency of oscillation using Barkhausen Criterion.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Wein-Bridge Oscillator Theory and Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Oscillator Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Non-inverting op-amp amplifier with closed-loop gain Av = 1 + \(Rf / R1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Feedback network: Lead-Lag Wein Bridge consisting of series R-C branch and parallel R-C) Tj
T*
(   branch.) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Feedback Factor Beta\(s\):) Tj
T*
(   - Series branch impedance: Zs = R + 1 / \(s * C\) = \(s*R*C + 1\) / \(s * C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Parallel branch admittance: Yp = 1/R + s*C = \(s*R*C + 1\) / R => Zp = R / \(s*R*C + 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage divider feedback factor:) Tj
T*
(   Beta\(s\) = Vf / Vout = Zp / \(Zs + Zp\) = [ R / \(sRC + 1\) ] / [ \(sRC + 1\)/sC + R/\(sRC + 1\) ].) Tj
T*
(   Beta\(s\) = \(s * R * C\) / [ \(s*R*C + 1\)^2 + s * R * C ] = \(s * R * C\) / [ s^2 * R^2 * C^2 + 3 * s) Tj
T*
(   * R * C + 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Frequency Domain Substitution \(s = j * omega\):) Tj
T*
(   - Beta\(j*omega\) = \(j * omega * R * C\) / [ \(1 - omega^2 * R^2 * C^2\) + j * 3 * omega * R * C ].) Tj
T*
(   4. Applying Barkhausen Criterion:) Tj
T*
(   - Phase Criterion: Loop phase shift must be zero \(Phase of Av * Beta = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   Since non-inverting amplifier has 0 deg phase, Beta\(j*omega\) must be purely real.) Tj
T*
(   Set imaginary real denominator term to zero:) Tj
T*
(   1 - omega_0^2 * R^2 * C^2 = 0 => omega_0^2 = 1 / \(R^2 * C^2\).) Tj
T*
(   Resonant Frequency: omega_0 = 1 / \(R * C\) => f_0 = 1 / \(2 * pi * R * C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Magnitude Criterion: Loop gain |Av * Beta| = 1.0 at resonance:) Tj
T*
(   At omega_0, Beta\(j*omega_0\) = \(j*omega_0*RC\) / \(j*3*omega_0*RC\) = 1 / 3.) Tj
T*
(   Av * Beta = Av * \(1 / 3\) = 1.0 => Av = 3.0.) Tj
T*
(   - Since Av = 1 + \(Rf / R1\) = 3.0:) Tj
T*
(   Rf / R1 = 2.0 => Rf = 2 * R1.) Tj
T*
(   - Non-linear amplitude stabilization \(thermistor, incandescent bulb, or back-to-back diodes\) is) Tj
T*
(   added in feedback to regulate gain at exactly 3.0.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
