(   - Upper Threshold Voltage: V_UT = beta * \(+Vsat\) = + beta * Vsat.) Tj
T*
(   - Lower Threshold Voltage: V_LT = beta * \(-Vsat\) = - beta * Vsat,) Tj
T*
(   where feedback fraction beta = R1 / \(R1 + R2\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Capacitor Charging and Discharging Transient Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Suppose Vout = +Vsat. Capacitor C charges toward +Vsat through resistor R from initial) Tj
T*
(   voltage -beta*Vsat:) Tj
T*
(   vc\(t\) = V_target + [ V_initial - V_target ] * exp\(- t / RC\)) Tj
T*
(   = +Vsat + [ -beta*Vsat - Vsat ] * exp\(- t / RC\)) Tj
T*
(   = Vsat * [ 1 - \(1 + beta\) * exp\(- t / RC\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - When vc\(t\) reaches +beta*Vsat at t = T1, inverting terminal voltage exceeds non-inverting) Tj
T*
(   terminal, snapping output to -Vsat.) Tj
T*
(   - Equating:) Tj
T*
(   beta * Vsat = Vsat * [ 1 - \(1 + beta\) * exp\(- T1 / RC\) ].) Tj
T*
(   \(1 + beta\) * exp\(- T1 / RC\) = 1 - beta.) Tj
T*
(   exp\(T1 / RC\) = \(1 + beta\) / \(1 - beta\) => T1 = R * C * ln[ \(1 + beta\) / \(1 - beta\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - The discharge half-cycle T2 is completely symmetrical: T2 = T1.) Tj
T*
(   4. Total Period and Frequency:) Tj
T*
(   - Total period: T = T1 + T2 = 2 * R * C * ln[ \(1 + beta\) / \(1 - beta\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Frequency of oscillation:) Tj
T*
(   f_0 = 1 / T = 1 / [ 2 * R * C * ln\( \(1 + beta\) / \(1 - beta\) \) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Special Case: If R1 = 1.16 * R2, beta = 0.462 and ln[\(1+beta\)/\(1-beta\)] = 1.0:) Tj
T*
(   T = 2 * R * C, and f_0 = 1 / \(2 * R * C\).) Tj
T*
