BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Triangular-Square Wave Generator circuit, deriving formulas for peak-to-peak amplitude and frequency.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Op-Amp Triangular and Square Wave Generator:) Tj
T*
(   1. Circuit Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Formed by a closed loop containing two stages:) Tj
T*
(   Stage 1: A Non-Inverting Schmitt Trigger \(Op-Amp A1 with resistors R1 and R2\).) Tj
T*
(   Stage 2: An Inverting Integrator \(Op-Amp A2 with input resistor R and feedback capacitor C\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Operating Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - When Schmitt trigger output V1 = +Vsat, integrator integrates negative constant voltage:) Tj
T*
(   Vout\(t\) = - \(1 / RC\) * Integral \(+Vsat\) dt = - \(Vsat / RC\) * t.) Tj
T*
(   - The triangular output Vout ramps linearly downward with constant slope -Vsat / RC.) Tj
T*
(   - Output Vout is fed back to the Schmitt trigger input. When Vout reaches the lower threshold) Tj
T*
(   V_LT, the Schmitt trigger snaps to -Vsat.) Tj
T*
(   - Now V1 = -Vsat; integrator ramps linearly upward with slope +Vsat / RC until Vout reaches) Tj
T*
(   upper threshold V_UT, causing Schmitt trigger to switch back to +Vsat.) Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of Triangular Wave Amplitude:) Tj
T*
(   - Schmitt switching occurs when V+ = 0:) Tj
T*
(   \(V1 * R2 + Vout * R1\) / \(R1 + R2\) = 0 => Vout = - V1 * \(R1 / R2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Peak-to-Peak Triangular Amplitude:) Tj
T*
(   V_pp = 2 * Vsat * \(R1 / R2\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Derivation of Frequency:) Tj
T*
(   - Ramp time for output to change by V_pp:) Tj
T*
(   Delta-V = V_pp = \(Vsat / RC\) * \(T / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   2 * Vsat * \(R1 / R2\) = \(Vsat / RC\) * \(T / 2\) => T / 2 = 2 * R * C * \(R1 / R2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total Period: T = 4 * R * C * \(R1 / R2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Frequency: f_0 = 1 / T = R2 / [ 4 * R1 * R * C ].) Tj
T*
(   - Produces synchronized square waves at Stage 1 and perfect linear triangular waves at Stage 2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

