(>> Solution to Question 11:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Slew Rate and derive the expression for Full-Power Bandwidth \(f_max\) of an operational amplifier.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Slew Rate and Large-Signal Bandwidth:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Definition:) Tj
T*
(   - Slew Rate \(SR\) is the maximum rate of change of output voltage that an op-amp can produce:) Tj
T*
(   SR = | dVout / dt |_max.) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Origin: Internally, op-amps contain an internal frequency-compensation capacitor Cc) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., 30 pF in 741\) charged by a differential input stage tail current source Itail.) Tj
T*
(   Maximum charging current is limited: SR = Itail / Cc.) Tj
T*
(   2. Distortion of Sinusoidal Signals:) Tj
T*
(   - Let output be a large sinusoidal voltage: vout\(t\) = Vp * sin\(2 * pi * f * t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Rate of change:) Tj
T*
(   dvout / dt = 2 * pi * f * Vp * cos\(2 * pi * f * t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Maximum rate of change occurs at zero-crossings:) Tj
T*
(   | dvout / dt |_max = 2 * pi * f * Vp.) Tj
T*
(   3. Full-Power Bandwidth \(f_max\):) Tj
T*
(   - To prevent slew-induced distortion \(where sine wave is distorted into a triangle wave\),) Tj
T*
(   maximum slope must not exceed SR:) Tj
T*
(   2 * pi * f * Vp <= SR.) Tj
T*
(   - Full-Power Bandwidth:) Tj
T*
(   f_max = SR / \(2 * pi * Vp\).) Tj
T*
(   - If an amplifier has SR = 0.5 V/us and delivers peak output Vp = 10 V:) Tj
T*
(   f_max = \(0.5 * 10^6 V/s\) / \(2 * pi * 10 V\) = 50,000 / \(2 * pi\) approx 7,958 Hz \(~8 kHz\).) Tj
T*
(   - Above 8 kHz, full-amplitude 10 V output signals distort into slew-rate-limited triangular) Tj
T*
(   waves.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
