(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Current-Feedback Operational Amplifiers \(CFOA\), comparing architecture, slew rate, and gain-bandwidth independence with VFOA.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Current-Feedback Operational Amplifiers \(CFOA\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage-Feedback Op-Amp \(VFOA\): High-impedance differential voltage input stage.) Tj
T*
(   - CFOA: Non-inverting input \(+\) is high impedance; an internal unity-gain buffer replicates V+) Tj
T*
(   at the inverting input \(-\), making the inverting input a low-impedance current-driven node.) Tj
T*
(   - Feedback current If entering inverting pin is mirrored into a high-impedance transimpedance) Tj
T*
(   node Zt\(s\) via current mirrors.) Tj
T*
(   2. Gain-Bandwidth Independence:) Tj
T*
(   - In standard VFOAs, Gain * Bandwidth = Constant. Increasing closed-loop gain reduces bandwidth) Tj
T*
(   proportionally.) Tj
T*
(   - In CFOAs, loop gain depends primarily on feedback resistor Rf and transimpedance Zt\(s\), and) Tj
T*
(   is independent of input resistor R1:) Tj
T*
(   omega_3dB approx 1 / \(Rf * Ct\).) Tj
T*
(   - Closed-loop gain is set by 1 + \(Rf / R1\). Gain can be varied simply by changing R1 without) Tj
T*
(   altering closed-loop bandwidth!) Tj
T*
(   3. Ultrafast Slew Rate:) Tj
T*
(   - VFOA slew rate is throttled by internal constant tail current Itail charging compensation) Tj
T*
(   capacitor.) Tj
T*
(   - In CFOA, transient input differences produce large proportional dynamic error currents) Tj
T*
(   directly from current mirrors on demand:) Tj
T*
(   Slew rate exceeds 1,000 to 3,000 V/microsecond!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
