/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 18:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Design a 50 Hz Active Notch Filter using a Twin-T network in an op-amp feedback configuration.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   50 Hz Active Twin-T Notch Filter Design:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operational Objective:) Tj
T*
(   - Reject 50 Hz power-line interference \(hum\) in biomedical instrumentation \(ECG, EEG\) and audio) Tj
T*
(   systems while passing all other frequencies unaltered.) Tj
T*
(   2. Symmetrical Twin-T Passive Network:) Tj
T*
(   - T-Section 1 \(Low-Pass T\): Two series resistors R with central shunt capacitor 2*C to ground.) Tj
T*
(   - T-Section 2 \(High-Pass T\): Two series capacitors C with central shunt resistor R/2 to ground.) Tj
T*
(   - Notch Frequency:) Tj
T*
(   f_0 = 1 / \(2 * pi * R * C\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Active Bootstrapped Configuration:) Tj
T*
(   - Passive Twin-T filters have very low Quality factor \(Q approx 0.25\), producing an excessively) Tj
T*
(   wide, sloppy rejection notch that attenuates adjacent valid signal frequencies.) Tj
T*
(   - To achieve high Q and a sharp notch, the neutral node of the Twin-T is connected to the) Tj
T*
(   output of a voltage follower buffer driven by a fraction k of the filter output.) Tj
T*
(   - Effective Quality Factor:) Tj
T*
(   Q = 1 / [ 4 * \(1 - k\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - As k -> 1, Q increases dramatically \(Q = 10 to 50\), yielding an extraordinarily sharp,) Tj
T*
(   surgical 50 Hz notch.) Tj
T*
