(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Tow-Thomas Biquad active filter and derive its transfer function.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Tow-Thomas Biquad Active Filter:) Tj
T*
(   1. Circuit Topology:) Tj
T*
(   - Consists of three operational amplifiers:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Op-Amp 1: Lossy inverting integrator with parallel damping resistor R1.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Op-Amp 2: Ideal inverting integrator.) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Op-Amp 3: Inverting unity-gain amplifier \(inverter\).) Tj
T*
(   - Connected in a closed ring loop providing overall negative feedback.) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - First integrator: V1 = - \(1 / s*C1\) * [ Vin/Rin + V1/R1 + V3/R2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Second integrator: V2 = - V1 / \(s * C2 * R\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inverter: V3 = - V2.) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting yields the standard biquadratic transfer function:) Tj
T*
(   H_BP\(s\) = - s * \(1 / Rin*C1\) / [ s^2 + s / \(R1*C1\) + 1 / \(R^2 * C1 * C2\) ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Advantages:) Tj
T*
(   - Unconditionally stable; independent tuning of gain, center frequency, and bandwidth; produces) Tj
T*
(   simultaneous bandpass and low-pass outputs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
