BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Sample-and-Hold \(S/H\) Amplifiers, defining acquisition time, aperture jitter, and droop rate.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Sample-and-Hold \(S/H\) Amplifier Systems:) Tj
T*
(   1. Function:) Tj
T*
(   - Freezes an analog input voltage level constant during the finite conversion time of an) Tj
T*
(   Analog-to-Digital Converter \(ADC\) to prevent amplitude distortion.) Tj
T*
(   2. Circuit Components:) Tj
T*
(   - Input unity-gain buffer op-amp, fast electronic analog switch \(MOSFET\), precision) Tj
T*
(   polystyrene/Teflon storage capacitor Ch, and output ultra-high-input-impedance buffer op-amp.) Tj
T*
(   3. Critical Dynamic Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   - Acquisition Time \(t_acq\): Time required after sample command for hold capacitor to charge and) Tj
T*
(   settle within specified error band \(+-0.01%\) of input voltage.) Tj
T*
(   - Aperture Time \(t_ap\): Propagation delay between hold command and physical opening of the) Tj
T*
(   switch.) Tj
T*
(   - Aperture Jitter \(t_j\): Sample-to-sample statistical uncertainty in aperture time. Limits) Tj
T*
(   maximum allowable signal frequency: f_max < 1 / \(2 * pi * t_j * 2^N\).) Tj
T*
(   - Droop Rate \(dV/dt\): Rate at which capacitor voltage decays during hold mode due to switch) Tj
T*
(   leakage and buffer input bias current: dV/dt = I_leak / Ch.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 23:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Wien-Bridge Oscillator Amplitude Stabilization mechanisms \(Diodes, JFET, and PTC Thermistors\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Wein-Bridge Amplitude Stabilization Techniques:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Gain Dilemma:) Tj
T*
(   - Barkhausen criterion strictly requires loop gain Av * Beta = 1.0 \(Av = 3.0\) for sustained) Tj
T*
(   sinusoidal oscillations.) Tj
T*
(   - If Av < 3.0, oscillations die out exponentially.) Tj
T*
(   - If Av > 3.0, oscillations grow exponentially until clipped by op-amp supply rails, producing) Tj
T*
(   severe harmonic distortion.) Tj
T*
(   2. Incandescent Lamp / PTC Thermistor Stabilization:) Tj
T*
(   - Tungsten lamp placed as resistor R1 in non-inverting gain feedback.) Tj
T*
(   - If oscillation amplitude grows, RMS current through lamp increases, heating the filament.) Tj
T*
ET

