(   - Diode D1 clamps capacitor C to ~0.7 V, preventing further charging.) Tj
T*
(   - Voltage divider establishes positive threshold V_UT = beta * \(+Vsat\) > 0.7 V.) Tj
T*
(   2. Triggering and Quasi-Stable State:) Tj
T*
(   - A negative trigger pulse applied to non-inverting terminal drives V+ below 0.7 V.) Tj
T*
(   - Op-amp output snaps instantaneously to -Vsat \(Quasi-Stable State\).) Tj
T*
(   - Positive feedback establishes negative threshold V_LT = - beta * Vsat.) Tj
T*
(   - Diode D1 becomes reverse biased. Capacitor C begins charging exponentially toward -Vsat) Tj
T*
(   through resistor R.) Tj
T*
(   3. Pulse Width Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Capacitor voltage charges from initial +0.7 V toward -Vsat:) Tj
T*
(   vc\(t\) = -Vsat + [ 0.7 - \(-Vsat\) ] * exp\(- t / RC\) approx -Vsat * [ 1 - exp\(- t / RC\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - When vc\(t\) crosses V_LT = - beta * Vsat at t = T_pulse, op-amp switches back to +Vsat.) Tj
T*
(   - Equating: - beta * Vsat = - Vsat * [ 1 - exp\(- T_pulse / RC\) ].) Tj
T*
(   exp\(- T_pulse / RC\) = 1 - beta => T_pulse = R * C * ln[ 1 / \(1 - beta\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Circuit returns to stable state and resets.) Tj
T*
