(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Active Inductor Simulation using Antoniou's General Impedance Converter \(GIC\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Antoniou's General Impedance Converter \(GIC\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Contains two operational amplifiers and five passive impedances \(Z1, Z2, Z3, Z4, Z5\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Driving-Point Input Impedance Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Analyzing node voltages and branch currents through virtual shorts:) Tj
T*
(   Z_in\(s\) = \(Z1 * Z3 * Z5\) / \(Z2 * Z4\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Synthesizing High-Q Grounded Inductor:) Tj
T*
(   - Select Z2 as a capacitor C \(Z2 = 1 / \(s*C\)\), and Z1, Z3, Z4, Z5 as resistors R1, R3, R4, R5:) Tj
T*
(   Z_in\(s\) = [ R1 * R3 * R5 ] / [ \(1 / s*C\) * R4 ] = s * [ \(R1 * R3 * R5 * C\) / R4 ].) Tj
T*
(   - This matches an ideal inductor impedance Z_in = s * L_eq, where:) Tj
T*
(   L_eq = \(R1 * R3 * R5 * C\) / R4.) Tj
T*
(   - Provides extremely high Quality factors \(Q > 500\), immune to magnetic saturation and core) Tj
T*
(   losses.) Tj
T*
